sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch05-18> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch05-18--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch05-18--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch05-18: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.37" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.368"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.5"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The least-area geometry can be tested the same way as other unduloid claims, but only by compiling images, and only for a few loricate genera. The denial of a protective purpose does not change any predicted measurement: a well-fitting unduloid can still be protective. Adsorption as the route by which the pellicle forms is likewise missing from the morphological record, so existing data reach only the shape proxy." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Fit loricas of Salpingoeca, Tintinnus and similar protozoa to the least-area surface available given their attachments, typically an unduloid, and ask whether form is fixed by that fit. A least-area match would support the geometric half. A protective purpose is not a separate measurable outcome, so it cannot be scored against the efficient-cause wording." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Lorica outlines are scattered in taxonomic plates.", "Protection is not an observable rival to set against a surface fit.", "Adsorption into the surface film, as against secreted wall material, is not recorded with the outline." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch05-18--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch05-18 by Grok 4.7: 0.45" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.45"^^xsd:double ;
